# Layout Catalogue

8 reusable layouts, built to work for any topic — not just LangChain — since these videos will
cover different subjects each time.

| ID | Name | Mode | Used for |
|---|---|---|---|
| `title_intro` | Title & Intro | Light | Opener: topic + short hook line |
| `narrator_note` | Narrator Attribution | Dark | A quote/statement, no real presenter video |
| `text_explanation` | Text & Explanation | Light | Main narration / concept explanation |
| `image_media` | Image & Media | Dark | Diagram, screenshot, or code snippet |
| `comparison` | Comparison | Light | Two things side by side |
| `step_by_step` | Step-by-Step | Light | A process or sequence |
| `key_takeaway` | Key Takeaway | Bright | One short, reinforced message |
| `closing_cta` | Closing / CTA | Dark | Wrap-up + next step |

## About the "presenter" layout

The task brief asks for a presenter-focused layout, but per the PRD a presenter face isn't
part of v1. So `narrator_note` isn't a person on screen — it's a statement/quote card, maybe
with a small generic icon next to it, not a photo or video of anyone. This covers the same
purpose (attributing a line to a voice/perspective) without needing real presenter footage. If
that changes later, this layout can just get a video field added on top.

## Why only 8 layouts

Keeping the set small on purpose. Visual variety across different videos should come from the
content — different text, different images — not from making a new layout for every topic.
That keeps things consistent and also easier to actually build and maintain.

## How a layout gets picked

The Scene Planner sends a `layout` field (a string) per scene. See
`04_scene_planner_mapping.md` for exactly how that gets resolved and filled in.